spes UFS log-only mode (0178): persistent console log with rd=md0, writes only in the log area.

With rd=md0 the UFS was only started by the read-only storage probe (spesufsprobe=1), so the
diagnostic profiles (touch, gpu-display, ...) could never use sweetlog. Boot-arg spesufslog=1 (rd=md0,
spes platform) starts the UFS in a log-only mode: SCSI limited to TEST UNIT READY, READ(10),
WRITE(10) and SYNCHRONIZE CACHE, and ufs_write_blocks accepts a write only if every block lies in the
log area = the last 1 + 4 MiB / 4 KiB blocks of the partition, computed at run time from the GPT
entry (first/last LBA) - the area sweet_log_thread writes (a _Static_assert ties the two sizes).
The bounds live in bsd/dev/spes_ufs_log.h without kernel headers; tests/test_spes_ufs_log.py
compiles that file from this patch on the host and checks the edge cases. ufsrw stays 0; writes to
/dev/ufsroot0 from userspace are refused the same way. Off by default.
After the log starts, the log-only init returns like the read-only probe: no sampling, touch,
cpufreq, amp or key drivers. Only the opt-in probes spes_vib_init (spesvib=) and spes_usb_probe
(spesusb=1) are called, which do nothing without their boot-args.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/spes_ufs_log.h b/bsd/dev/spes_ufs_log.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1b672c9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/bsd/dev/spes_ufs_log.h
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+/*
+ * 0178: bounds of the UFS log-only mode (boot-arg spesufslog=1), kept free of kernel headers so
+ * tests/test_spes_ufs_log.py compiles this very file on the host.
+ *
+ * first/nblocks come from the GPT entry of the partition at run time (sweet_ufs.c,
+ * ufs_find_partition); log_blocks is SWEET_LOG_BLOCKS (1 header + 4 MiB of 4 KiB blocks).
+ * Nothing here is a fixed block number.
+ */
+#ifndef SPES_UFS_LOG_H
+#define SPES_UFS_LOG_H
+
+/* First block of the log area: the last log_blocks blocks of the partition, or 0 (no log area). */
+static inline uint64_t
+spes_ufs_log_lo(uint64_t first, uint64_t nblocks, uint64_t log_blocks)
+{
+	if (log_blocks == 0 || nblocks < 2 * log_blocks || first > UINT64_MAX - nblocks) {
+		return 0;
+	}
+	return first + nblocks - log_blocks;
+}
+
+/*
+ * true only if all count blocks from lba lie in [log_lo, first + nblocks). Written without
+ * lba + count so that no sum can wrap.
+ */
+static inline bool
+spes_ufs_log_write_ok(uint64_t lba, uint64_t count, uint64_t first, uint64_t nblocks, uint64_t log_lo)
+{
+	if (count == 0 || nblocks == 0 || log_lo == 0 || log_lo < first || log_lo - first >= nblocks) {
+		return false;
+	}
+	if (lba < log_lo || lba - first >= nblocks) {
+		return false;
+	}
+	return count <= nblocks - (lba - first);
+}
+
+#endif /* SPES_UFS_LOG_H */
